# The SBCL source this tree builds its own SBCL binaries from (#1251).
#
# Ouranos builds SBCL from source and publishes the binaries as release assets of this
# repository, so that setup does not depend on SourceForge, which refuses SBCL downloads to
# some locations (#1216), and so that the project keeps working if SBCL's upstream stops
# publishing binaries. The source comes from codelisperer/sbcl, a fork of github.com/sbcl/sbcl
# (the official mirror of SBCL's git repository) that carries every release tag and no patches
# of our own.
#
# The build is .github/workflows/sbcl-build.yml, which runs scripts/build-sbcl.sh on each
# platform. That script clones `repo' at `tag', refuses the checkout unless its commit is
# `commit', and builds with the options written in the script.
#
# `release' numbers our builds of one SBCL version. The release tag is
# sbcl-v<version>-ouranos.<release>, and the asset names carry the same string, for example
# sbcl-2.6.10-ouranos.1-x86-64-linux-binary.tar.bz2. A rebuild of the same version with
# different options, or from a different host Lisp, takes the next release number, so that a
# checksum pinned for one build never names a different file.
#
# Until setup downloads these builds (#1251, step 5), scripts/versions.env still pins the
# SourceForge binary of SBCL_VERSION. The two versions can differ while that is so.
#
# To adopt a new SBCL release:
#   1. git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/codelisperer/sbcl sbcl-X.Y.Z
#      (the fork's tag sync brings new upstream tags in; compare with
#       git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/sbcl/sbcl sbcl-X.Y.Z, which must agree)
#   2. update version, tag and commit below, and set release back to 1
#   3. run the workflow (its header says how) and read every leg's test and gate results
#      before publishing.

version 2.6.10
repo    https://github.com/codelisperer/sbcl
tag     sbcl-2.6.10
commit  ee8952af37ab5a2a2408e7bddd966f2a903ffe9d
release 1

# The commit is the one both github.com/sbcl/sbcl and codelisperer/sbcl give for the tag
# sbcl-2.6.10, read with `git ls-remote --tags' on 2026-11-15 by the maintainer (#1251). A
# git commit identifies its tree, so no separate checksum of the source is pinned.

# --- staying current -------------------------------------------------------
#
# SBCL has no security advisory feed. It lists every change in a release, fixes for security
# problems included, in the NEWS file at the top of its source tree. REVIEWED is the date
# someone last read the NEWS entries up to and including this pin's version. On 2026-11-16
# the 2.6.10 entry listed no security fix; it lists fixes for miscompilations (DPB and
# (SETF LDB), conversions to UTF-8) and for heap corruption in :weakness :key hash tables.

advisories https://github.com/sbcl/sbcl/blob/master/NEWS
reviewed   2026-11-16
